        "type": "note",
        "x": 0.09914943033803082,
        "y": 0.2016171615246694,
        "text": "children and\ngrandchildren,\nhis continuation"
      },
      {
        "id": "325f2cd8-f8da-4265-9062-ea77bf61c590",
        "type": "note",
        "x": 0.14511023329013975,
        "y": 0.09039451313980004,
        "text": "the idea that the only reason we die is because we labor\nand that if we never grew up, if we stayed nimble, childish, foolish, we could live forever\nlike the thought that all old things are tough, hardened, strong, but young things are soft, nimble, weak"
      },
      {
        "id": "2d530229-d856-4039-8c2a-6b766b9be75c",
        "type": "note",
        "x": 0.11013240549350527,
        "y": 0.3020413255270136,
        "text": "What is the cares of the Father of the Family? Why does he care that this small thing may outlive him? The fact that literally \nliving longer is better continuation than children? "
      }
    ]
